# Git dual remote push

When pushing to git, always push the current branch to **both** remotes:

1. **GitHub (origin):** `https://github.com/vilanovax/wibecur.git`
2. **Hamgit:** `https://hamgit.ir/ramtinica/wibe.git`

`origin` is configured with two push URLs, so `git push origin HEAD` pushes to both.

Also run `git push hamgit HEAD` if dual push on origin fails for Hamgit.

Do not commit or push the nested `wibe/` directory (embedded repo).
